%% FINAL v2: processScores, identical for every source. Talks only to ports.
%% Reservation = a time-limited LEASE written in a short transaction (not a row lock held during the work).
%% Files move through a temporary workspace on disk and are streamed, so memory use does not grow with file size.

sequenceDiagram
    actor Op as Operator
    participant Core as core: processScores
    participant Repo as CatalogRepository
    participant WS as TempWorkspace
    participant Source as CatalogSource
    participant Rend as ScoreRenderer
    participant Store as ScoreStorage

    Op->>Core: npm run scores:download -- --limit N
    Core->>Repo: claimFiles(workerId, N, lease 15 min)
    Note over Repo: one short transaction: SKIP LOCKED picks free rows, sets status = processing, lease_owner, lease_expires_at, attempts + 1, then COMMIT
    Repo-->>Core: claimed files with licence, evidence and source policy

    loop each claimed file
        Core->>Core: licencePolicy (default deny)
        alt not allowed
            Core->>Repo: finish(file, rejected, reason) only while the lease is ours
        else allowed
            Core->>WS: create a private temp folder for this file
            Core->>Source: fetchFile(ref, tempPath, maxBytes) streamed to disk
            opt format is not PDF (e.g. .mscx)
                Core->>Rend: toPdf(inputPath, outputPath, timeout)
            end
            Core->>WS: inspect(pdfPath): %PDF- header, size, sha256 (streamed)
            Core->>Repo: renewLease(file, workerId)
            Core->>Store: exists(key)
            opt not stored yet
                Core->>Store: put(key, stream from file, size, sha256)
            end
            Core->>Repo: finish(file, stored, sha256, size, key) only while the lease is ours
            Core->>WS: delete the temp folder
        end
    end
    Note over Core,Store: Temporary error: back to pending with next_attempt_at (failed after max attempts). Crash: the lease expires and the file is claimed again, exists(key) prevents a second upload.
